Here is a complete, self-contained Node.js web application using Express and SQLite. 

SQLite's built-in locking mechanism, paired with an **exclusive, atomic database transaction**, guarantees that simultaneous requests cannot overbook beyond 20 seats and cannot insert duplicate emails.

### 1. Setup

Create a new directory, navigate into it, and install dependencies:

```bash
mkdir workshop-signup
cd workshop-signup
npm init -y
npm install express better-sqlite3
```

> **Why `better-sqlite3`?** It is synchronous and runs within standard, rigorous SQLite transactions (`BEGIN IMMEDIATE`), avoiding the race conditions that asynchronous database drivers can introduce during concurrent writes.

---

### 2. The Application (`server.js`)

Save the following code as `server.js`:

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const Database = require('better-sqlite3');

const app = express();
const db = new Database('workshop.db');

const TOTAL_SEATS = 20;

// Enable WAL mode for high concurrency between reads and writes
db.pragma('journal_mode = WAL');

// Initialize database table
db.exec(`
  CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS signups (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
    name TEXT NOT NULL,
    email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE COLLATE NOCASE,
    created_at DATETIME DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
  )
`);

// Prepared statements
const countStmt = db.prepare('SELECT COUNT(*) AS count FROM signups');
const insertStmt = db.prepare('INSERT INTO signups (name, email) VALUES (?, ?)');

/**
 * ATOMIC TRANSACTION
 * db.transaction() with 'immediate' acquires a reserved lock immediately.
 * This guarantees no other request can read the seat count and insert
 * between this transaction's check and insert steps.
 */
const registerUser = db.transaction((name, email) => {
  const { count } = countStmt.get();

  if (count >= TOTAL_SEATS) {
    const error = new Error('Workshop is fully booked.');
    error.code = 'FULL';
    throw error;
  }

  insertStmt.run(name, email);
  return TOTAL_SEATS - (count + 1);
});

app.use(express.json());

// API: Get remaining seat count (Privacy safe: no personal data returned)
app.get('/api/status', (req, res) => {
  const { count } = countStmt.get();
  res.json({
    totalSeats: TOTAL_SEATS,
    seatsRemaining: Math.max(0, TOTAL_SEATS - count),
  });
});

// API: Register for a seat
app.post('/api/signup', (req, res) => {
  let { name, email } = req.body;

  if (!name || !email) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Name and email are required.' });
  }

  name = name.trim();
  email = email.trim().toLowerCase();

  // Basic email pattern check
  const emailRegex = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
  if (!emailRegex.test(email)) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Invalid email address.' });
  }

  try {
    // Run the atomic transaction
    const seatsLeft = registerUser.immediate(name, email);
    return res.status(201).json({
      message: 'Seat confirmed! See you at the workshop.',
      seatsRemaining: seatsLeft,
    });
  } catch (err) {
    // Handle database UNIQUE constraint violation
    if (err.code === 'SQLITE_CONSTRAINT_UNIQUE') {
      return res.status(409).json({ error: 'This email has already registered.' });
    }
    // Handle capacity reached
    if (err.code === 'FULL') {
      return res.status(409).json({ error: 'Sorry, the workshop is now full.' });
    }
    console.error('Registration error:', err);
    return res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error.' });
  }
});

// Serve frontend UI
app.get('/', (req, res) => {
  res.send(`
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Workshop Registration</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: center; min-height: 100vh; margin: 0; background: #f4f6f8; }
    .card { background: white; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); width: 100%; max-width: 400px; }
    h1 { margin-top: 0; font-size: 1.5rem; text-align: center; }
    .seats-badge { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-weight: bold; color: #2563eb; }
    .form-group { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    label { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.25rem; font-size: 0.875rem; color: #374151; }
    input { width: 100%; padding: 0.5rem; border: 1px solid #d1d5db; border-radius: 4px; box-sizing: border-box; }
    button { width: 100%; padding: 0.75rem; background: #2563eb; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 4px; font-weight: bold; cursor: pointer; }
    button:disabled { background: #9ca3af; cursor: not-allowed; }
    .msg { margin-top: 1rem; padding: 0.75rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.875rem; text-align: center; }
    .success { background: #dcfce7; color: #166534; }
    .error { background: #fee2e2; color: #991b1b; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="card">
    <h1>Workshop Sign-up</h1>
    <div class="seats-badge" id="seatStatus">Loading seats...</div>

    <form id="signupForm">
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="name">Full Name</label>
        <input type="text" id="name" required autocomplete="name" />
      </div>
      <div class="form-group">
        <label for="email">Email Address</label>
        <input type="email" id="email" required autocomplete="email" />
      </div>
      <button type="submit" id="submitBtn">Reserve Seat</button>
    </form>
    <div id="message"></div>
  </div>

  <script>
    async function updateStatus() {
      const res = await fetch('/api/status');
      const data = await res.json();
      const statusEl = document.getElementById('seatStatus');
      const btn = document.getElementById('submitBtn');

      if (data.seatsRemaining <= 0) {
        statusEl.textContent = 'Workshop is Full (0 / ' + data.totalSeats + ' seats left)';
        statusEl.style.color = '#dc2626';
        btn.disabled = true;
      } else {
        statusEl.textContent = data.seatsRemaining + ' of ' + data.totalSeats + ' seats remaining';
        btn.disabled = false;
      }
    }

    document.getElementById('signupForm').addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();
      const messageEl = document.getElementById('message');
      const btn = document.getElementById('submitBtn');
      messageEl.className = '';
      messageEl.textContent = '';
      btn.disabled = true;

      const payload = {
        name: document.getElementById('name').value,
        email: document.getElementById('email').value
      };

      try {
        const res = await fetch('/api/signup', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify(payload)
        });
        const data = await res.json();

        if (res.ok) {
          messageEl.className = 'msg success';
          messageEl.textContent = data.message;
          document.getElementById('signupForm').reset();
        } else {
          messageEl.className = 'msg error';
          messageEl.textContent = data.error;
        }
      } catch (err) {
        messageEl.className = 'msg error';
        messageEl.textContent = 'Network error. Please try again.';
      } finally {
        updateStatus();
      }
    });

    updateStatus();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
  `);
});

const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;
app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server listening at http://localhost:${PORT}`);
});
```

---

### 3. Run the App

```bash
node server.js
```
Open your browser and visit **`http://localhost:3000`**.

---

### How Requirements Are Met

1. **Email Uniqueness:** The table has a `UNIQUE` constraint on the `email` column with `COLLATE NOCASE`. Attempting to register the same email address (even with different capitalization, e.g., `user@test.com` vs `USER@test.com`) is rejected with a `409 Conflict`.
2. **Privacy:** The frontend never fetches any user data. The `/api/status` endpoint only returns the total count of available seats, ensuring participant lists are not exposed to the public.
3. **Atomic Concurrency Protection:** 
   - `registerUser.immediate(...)` uses SQLite's `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` statement.
   - When requests hit the server concurrently, the first one locks the database for write access. Subsequent requests wait their turn; they cannot read an outdated seat count while an insertion is taking place. Once 20 seats are committed, any pending or future transaction hits `count >= TOTAL_SEATS` and aborts.

